course: dictionary
lesson: 12577
title: Diminutive: small and sweet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diminutive thing is very small or short. «The diminutive kitten fitted in my hand.» The word diminutive tells you the kitten was tiny.
explain: In grammar, a diminutive is a small form of a word, often with an ending such as -let, -ling, -ette or -ie. A duckling is a small duck, and a booklet is a small book.
explain: Diminutives can also show affection. «Billy» is a diminutive of William, and «Kate» is a diminutive of Katherine. People often use them for friends and family.
fact: Diminutive means very small or short.
fact: A diminutive is also a small form of a word or name, such as «piglet» or «Billy».
fact: The endings -let, -ling, -ette and -ie can make a word mean small: «booklet», «gosling», «kitchenette», «doggie».
fact: «Billy» is a diminutive of William, and «Mick» is a diminutive of Michael.
fact: A diminutive figure is a small person or creature in a story.
exercise: «The diminutive mouse hid under the sofa.» What does diminutive mean here? | *Very small | Very loud | Very hungry | Very old
exercise: Which word is a small form of pig? | pigsty | bacon | *piglet | pigeon
exercise: Mum calls her son Billy. Billy is a diminutive of which name? | Walter | Wilfred | Wendy | *William
test: Which ending makes kitchen mean a small kitchen? | -est | -ness | -ful | *-ette
test: Which one is a diminutive figure in a story? | A loud drum | A huge mountain | *A tiny fairy | A tall giant
exam: Which name is a diminutive of Michael? | Machine | Michigan | *Mick | Michaelmas
